<title>POLAND: Carlsberg wants Okocim to up mkt share.</title>
<headline>Carlsberg wants Okocim to up mkt share.</headline>
<dateline>BRZESKO, Poland 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's Carlsberg, the main shareholder of Polish brewer Okocim SA, said it wants the brewer to increase its market share to over 10 percent this year from the current 8.4 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Carlsberg, as the biggest shareholder, wants a strategy of development in Okocim that will increase the firm's domestic market share from 8.4 percent to over 10 percent in 1997,&quot; Carlsberg official Finn Jakobsen said.</p>
<p>Jakobsen made the remark to Okocim's shareholders' meeting, but did not give any details on the strategy.</p>
<p>Carlsberg has 31.8 percent in Okocim.</p>
<p>Okocim's deputy president Krzysztof Czwartkiewicz, also present, said Carlsberg beer produced by Okocim would enter the Polish market in June.</p>
<p>-- Wojciech Zurawski +48 22 653 9700</p>
